@page "/privacy"
@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptions<Candle_Obsession.Services.ShopOptions> ShopOpts
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How Candle Obsession collects, uses and protects your personal data when you order handmade candles, and your rights under the GDPR.";

    var shop = ShopOpts.Value;
    var couriers = shop.DeliveryMethods.Where(m => m.IsAvailable && m.Requires != "none").Select(m => m.Name).ToList();
}
<article class="info-page">
    <header class="info-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">CUSTOMER CARE</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="info-updated">Last updated: <mark>[TODO: date]</mark></p>
    </header>
    <partial name="_DraftNotice" />
    <div class="prose">
        <section>
            <h2>The short version</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>We only collect what we need to make, deliver and support your order.</li>
                <li>We don't use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
                <li>We never see or store your full card details.</li>
                <li>We never sell your data.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Who we are</h2>
            <p>The controller responsible for your personal data is:</p>
            <address>
                <strong>@Or(shop.LegalName, "legal name of the business owner or company")</strong>, trading as @shop.Name<br />
                @Or(shop.TradingAddress, "business address")<br />
                Registration no.: @Or(shop.RegistrationNumber, "registration number")<br />
                Email: @Or(shop.ContactEmail, "contact email")<br />
                Phone: @Or(shop.ContactPhone, "contact phone")
            </address>
            <p>We are a small business and have not appointed a Data Protection Officer. <mark>[TODO: confirm]</mark> For any privacy question, just contact us using the details above.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>What we collect</h2>
            <p>When you place an order we ask for:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>your name, email address and phone number;</li>
                <li>your delivery address, or the BOX NOW locker you chose (nothing for local pickup);</li>
                <li>what you ordered, the price, delivery and payment method you chose, and the order status;</li>
                <li>a gift message, if you add one (it may include the recipient's name);</li>
                <li>any notes you add to your order, such as personalisation details;</li>
                <li>if you buy a wine gift box: confirmation that you are at least @shop.AlcoholMinimumAge years old.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If you contact us by email, phone or Instagram, we also keep what you send us.</p>
            <p>When you visit the site, our hosting provider may automatically record technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the pages requested, for security and to keep the site running. <mark>[TODO: confirm what the hosting provider logs and for how long]</mark></p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Why we use it, and the legal basis</h2>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Processing, making, delivering and supporting your order; handling returns and refunds</td><td>Performance of a contract, Art. 6(1)(b)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Keeping invoices and accounting records</td><td>Legal obligation, Art. 6(1)(c)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Checking the age limit for alcohol products</td><td>Legal obligation, Art. 6(1)(c) <mark>[TODO: confirm once licensing is clarified]</mark></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Answering your messages, preventing fraud, keeping the site secure, handling disputes</td><td>Our legitimate interests, Art. 6(1)(f)</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p>We do not send marketing emails. <mark>[TODO: if a newsletter is added later, it needs separate opt-in consent]</mark></p>
            <p>We do not make decisions about you by automated means or build profiles.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
            <p>We don't use any analytics, advertising or social media tracking cookies.</p>
            <p>The site uses your browser's local storage only for:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>your shopping cart</strong>, so the items you add stay in your basket while you shop;</li>
                <li><strong>your "evening mode" preference</strong>, if you switch it on, so the site remembers how you like it to look.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>This information stays on your device. It is not used to track you and is not shared with anyone. Because it is only used to provide something you asked for, EU rules (Article 5(3) of the ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC) do not require a consent banner for it. <mark>[TODO: verify the evening-mode preference is treated as strictly necessary/functional under Cypriot rules]</mark></p>
            <p>The checkout form may also set a technical security cookie that protects against forged form submissions. It is strictly necessary and contains no personal data. If you are the shop owner and sign in to the admin area, a sign-in cookie (co_admin) is also set. Ordinary shoppers never receive it. <mark>[TODO: developer to confirm the full list of cookies the site sets]</mark></p>
            <p>You can clear local storage and cookies at any time in your browser settings. This will empty your cart.</p>
            <p>All of the site's scripts, fonts and icons are served from our own server. We don't load anything from third-party content networks, font services or trackers.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Payments</h2>
            <p>Card payments are handled by our payment provider, <mark>[TODO: name of the card payment provider]</mark>, on their secure page. We never see or store your full card number or security code. We only receive confirmation that the payment went through.</p>
            <p>If you pay with Revolut, Revolut processes your payment under its own privacy policy. If you pay cash, we only record that the order was paid.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
            <p>We only share what each of these needs to do their job:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Couriers</strong>@if (couriers.Count > 0) { <text> (@string.Join(", ", couriers))</text> }: your name, phone, email and delivery address or locker, to deliver your parcel.</li>
                <li><strong>Our payment provider</strong>: <mark>[TODO: name]</mark>.</li>
                <li><strong>Our website hosting provider</strong>: <mark>[TODO: name and location]</mark>, which stores the site and the order database.</li>
                <li><strong>Our email provider</strong>: <mark>[TODO: name]</mark>, used to send order confirmations and replies.</li>
                <li><strong>Our accountant</strong> and, where the law requires, the tax authorities. <mark>[TODO: confirm]</mark></li>
            </ul>
            <p>Service providers that process data for us act on our instructions under a data processing agreement. <mark>[TODO: confirm agreements are in place]</mark></p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Transfers outside the EU</h2>
            <p><mark>[TODO: depends on the hosting, email and payment providers. If any of them stores data outside the EU/EEA, name the country and the safeguard used (e.g. EU adequacy decision or Standard Contractual Clauses). If everything stays in the EU, say so here.]</mark></p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Order and invoice records</strong>: as long as Cypriot accounting and tax law requires. <mark>[TODO: verify with accountant; sources commonly cite at least 6 years, and some official guidance mentions 7 years]</mark></li>
                <li><strong>Gift messages and order notes</strong>: <mark>[TODO: e.g. deleted 3 months after delivery]</mark></li>
                <li><strong>Messages you send us</strong>: <mark>[TODO: e.g. 2 years after the last contact]</mark></li>
                <li><strong>Server logs</strong>: <mark>[TODO: per hosting provider]</mark></li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Your rights</h2>
            <p>Under the GDPR you can ask us to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>give you a copy of your personal data (access);</li>
                <li>correct data that is wrong;</li>
                <li>delete your data, where we no longer need to keep it;</li>
                <li>limit how we use it;</li>
                <li>give you your data in a portable format;</li>
                <li>stop using it for purposes based on our legitimate interests (objection).</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Contact us at @Or(shop.ContactEmail, "contact email") to use any of these rights. We will reply within one month. We may need to confirm your identity first. Some data, such as invoices, we must keep by law even if you ask us to delete it.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Complaints</h2>
            <p>If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, please tell us first so we can put it right. You also have the right to complain to the data protection authority in Cyprus, the <strong>Office of the Commissioner for Personal Data Protection</strong>: <a href="https://www.dataprotection.gov.cy/">www.dataprotection.gov.cy</a>, or to the authority in the EU country where you live.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Changes</h2>
            <p>If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of this page.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</article>

@functions {
    private static Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html.IHtmlContent Or(string? value, string todo) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value)
            ? new Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html.HtmlString("<mark>[TODO: " + System.Net.WebUtility.HtmlEncode(todo) + "]</mark>")
            : new Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html.HtmlString(System.Net.WebUtility.HtmlEncode(value));
}
